      "paragraph_number": 128,
      "text": "Values are presented as median (interquartile range) or n (%). Percentages were calculated using available nonmissing observations; available n is shown where it differs from 445. Clinical manifestations were not mutually exclusive. Metabolic comorbidities were defined as the presence of obesity, hypertension or diabetes mellitus; obesity was defined as BMI ≥28 kg/m². Retained viral-marker coding, source-scale limitations and derived-index definitions are provided in Supplementary Table S3A and Supplementary Note M1. Abbreviations: BMI, body mass index; HBV, hepatitis B virus; DNA, deoxyribonucleic acid; HBeAg, hepatitis B e antigen; anti-HBe, antibody to hepatitis B e antigen; HBsAg, hepatitis B surface antigen; EGVH, esophagogastric variceal hemorrhage; SBP, spontaneous bacterial peritonitis; HE, hepatic encephalopathy; HRS, hepatorenal syndrome; ALT, alanine aminotransferase; AST, aspartate aminotransferase; ALP, alkaline phosphatase; GGT, gamma-glutamyl transferase; INR, international normalized ratio; PT, prothrombin time; PTA, prothrombin activity; WBC, white blood cell count; MELD-Na, Model for End-Stage Liver Disease-sodium; ALBI, albumin-bilirubin score; FIB-4, fibrosis-4 index.",
